             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <p>Kaal Bhairav is a fierce and powerful form of Lord Shiva, who is known to protect his devotees from fear, evil forces, and harmful energies. Kaal Bhairav Anushthan is an important ritual dedicated to worshiping Lord Bhairav, who is revered as the guardian of time and destroyer of negative energies. This pooja is performed to bring about protection, fearlessness, and freedom from obstacles in one's life.</p>
                 <p>It is performed to appease Kaal Bhairav, who is believed to have the power to remove doshas, black magic, and evil forces from one's life, while also granting wisdom, prosperity, and spiritual growth.</p>
             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>Why Perform Kaal Bhairav Anushthan?</b>
                 <ul>
                     <li>To remove fear, negativity, and evil influences in life</li>
                     <li>To seek protection from dangers, accidents, and misfortunes</li>
                     <li>To remove Black Magic, evil spirits, and spiritual blockages</li>
                     <li>To attract wealth, health, and happiness</li>
                     <li>To gain mental strength and fearless attitude</li>
                     <li>To receive blessings for personal and professional growth</li>
                     <li>To clear debt and financial issues</li>
                     <li>To fulfill spiritual aspirations and attain Moksha (liberation)</li>
                 </ul>
             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>Rituals Performed in Kaal Bhairav Anushthan:
Sankalp and Ganapati Invocation
</b>
                 <p>Kalash Sthapana (Installation of Sacred Water Pot)</p>
                 <p>Kaal Bhairav Mantras Chanting (ॐ कालभैरवाय नमः)</p>
                 <p>Pujan of Kaal Bhairav with Bael Patra, Bilva Leaves, and Ghee</p>
                 <p>Offering of Mustard Oil, Black Sesame Seeds, and Red Flowers</p>
                 <p>Recitation of Kaal Bhairav Ashtakshari Mantra</p>
                 <p>Havan (Fire Ritual) using Herbs, Ghee, and Samidha</p>
                 <p>Prayers for Protection from negative energies</p>
                 <p>Aarti and Bhajans to please Lord Bhairav</p>
                 <p>Brahmin Bhojan (Feeding the Priests) as an act of charity</p>
